{Game Krassowizkij, J (2450)–Braun, G (2400), 2021.} 25. h4 {[%cal Gh4h5] White launches an attack. Can Black defend against it?} d4 $1 {No, but Black does not have to. By attacking as well, Black combines defense with an attempt to win. Counterplay means counterattacking instead of waiting passively.} 26. cxd4 Nxd4 27. Qg4 Qb7 {It is already unclear who is better here.} 28. Re3 Nf5 29. h5 $5 {White sacrifices the exchange to build up the initiative.} Nxe3 30. Bxe3 {The position has now changed permanently. Previously the struggle was about the initiative; now it is Black's material advantage against White's attack. Both sides must adapt their plans and style of play.}
Nd3 31. hxg6 Nxe5 32. gxf7+ $36 *

